        <p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1F497D">Jessica,<o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1F497D">Trying to
            follow two different documentations that reference each
            other and a video on an older ADT and Eclipse versions is a
            bit of a challenge to get things setup. I am testing
            different approaches on my own in order to get a better
            understanding of what is going on.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1F497D">So to be clear:<o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#1F497D"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoListParagraph"
          style="text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span
            style="color:#1F497D"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">1.<span
                style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
              </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span
            style="color:#1F497D">Download the ADT 1.3 installer<o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoListParagraph"
          style="text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span
            style="color:#1F497D"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">2.<span
                style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
              </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span
            style="color:#1F497D">Extract the install, don&#8217;t make any
            changes to the adt-install.conf file &#8211; just install the ARM<o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoListParagraph"
          style="text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span
            style="color:#1F497D"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">3.<span
                style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
              </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span
            style="color:#1F497D">Run the ADT installer, which should
            install the tool chain<o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoListParagraph"
          style="text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span
            style="color:#1F497D"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">4.<span
                style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
              </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span
            style="color:#1F497D">Download the core-image-sato-sdk 1.3
            image
            <o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoListParagraph"
          style="text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span
            style="color:#1F497D"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">5.<span
                style="font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
              </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span
            style="color:#1F497D">Use the runqemu-extract-sdk to extract
            to the sysroot defined by ADT installer<o:p></o:p></span></p>
